CHAPTER.VERS:
I commend to you

          {+}
         Phoebe, our sister, and who is a servant of the church that is at Cenchreae:

that you

          {+}
         receive her in the Lord, worthily of the saints, and that you

          {+}
         assist her in whatever matter she may have need of you

          {+}
        : for she herself also has been a helper of many, and of my own self.

Greet Mary, who bestowed much labor on you

          {+}
        .

Greet one another with a holy kiss. All the churches of Christ greet you

          {+}
        .

Now I urge you

          {+}
        , brothers, mark those who are causing the divisions and occasions of stumbling, contrary to the doctrine which you

          {+}
         learned: and turn away from them.

For your

          {+}
         obedience has come abroad to all men. I rejoice therefore over you

          {+}
        : but I would have you

          {+}
         wise to that which is good, and simple to that which is evil.

And the God of peace will bruise Satan under your

          {+}
         feet shortly. The grace of our Lord Jesus be with you

          {+}
        .

Timothy my coworker greets you

          {+}
        ; and Lucius and Jason and Sosipater, my kinsmen.

I Tertius, who write the letter, greet you

          {+}
         in the Lord.

Gaius my host, and of the whole church, greets you

          {+}
        . Erastus the treasurer of the city greets you

          {+}
        , and Quartus the brother.

Now to him who is able to establish you

          {+}
         according to my good news and the preaching of Jesus Christ, according to the revelation of the mystery which has been kept in silence through eternal times,
